Refer to Marine Orders 504
7. What are FOUR emergency situations for which crew should receive inductions?
[[ANSWER: The emergency plan must include procedures for responding to each of the following situations that is relevant to the vessel and its operation:

(a)   fire;
(b)   a person overboard or unaccountably missing;
(c)   a personal injury or other medical emergency;
(d)   master incapacitated;
(e)   loss of steering;
(f)    vessel collision;
(g)   vessel grounding;
(h)   vessel flooding;
(i)    adverse weather or water conditions;
(j)    any other circumstance identified by the risk assessment that may require an emergency response.]]

